TOPIC: Why Monitoring is Required

If a server goes down in Kubernetes, logs get deleted automatically. Without centralized logging, troubleshooting is impossible.

With 100+ machines, manually checking logs is not feasible.

Hackers can enter systems and delete logs. A centralized backup protects against this.

Storing all logs on individual servers increases machine size and cost.

SOLUTION: Centralized location for logs with continuous monitoring.

TYPES OF MONITORING:

Infrastructure Monitoring - CPU, memory, disk, network, VMs, containers, on-premises servers.

Application Monitoring - Application logs, access logs, APIs, SLAs, transactions, error logs, performance, user response.

Network Monitoring - Throughput, packet loss, data input/output, network outages. Often uses agentless methods like SNMP or APIs.

